{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr5iWC4vRbFDnmPKTpPH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't read any file contents, so this diagnosis rests on the report and on how this NestJS boilerplate is usually laid out. The line numbers are estimates.\n\nThe symptoms point to an off-by-one-page error in the pagination offset. Page 1 skips 10 users and page 2 skips 20, so the offset is being computed as `page * limit` instead of `(page - 1) * limit`. With only the two seeded accounts, skipping 10 leaves nothing, which explains the empty list.\n\nThe offset is computed in the persistence layer's `findManyWithPagination`. A fresh install with seeded accounts most likely uses the relational (TypeORM) repository, so that is the first candidate. The document (Mongoose) repository is the second, in case the project runs on MongoDB."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":4773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":330},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c78a41c-b249-440b-a877-0ca773107fa9","uuid":"22312f9c-a01a-414d-8a6b-d8022d0b2073","timestamp":"2026-11-08T20:20:56.497Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr5iVzuSi8qke3ioRiDH"}
